    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172-a1-a2">

                <pb facs="0290" n="220" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg220"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Chambers,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-09-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 29, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to your letter of the 12th
                    instant, and previous correspondence, I am directed by the lords, &amp;c, to
                    transmit herewith, for the information of Earl Russell, copy of a report, No.
                    478, dated 25th instant, of the commissioners of customs relative to the supply
                    of cannon, &amp;c., to the gunboat No. 290.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. A. HAMILTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
